        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Hardened the local Hermes bridge server startup and `/healthz` response path.\n- Added fail-closed dry-run handling for Hermes bridge task execution and route contracts.\n- Added local bridge diagnostics plus unit coverage for startup health payloads.\n- Synced OpenClaw integration dependency snapshots on the fork branch through commit `9bb5f950b0`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node --import tsx` direct bridge contract checks passed for startup diagnostics, health payloads, dryRun=false blocking, and message preview-only behavior.\n- `node --import tsx` direct HTTP route checks passed for `status.health` and route-level dryRun=false blocking.\n- Live smoke verified `http://127.0.0.1:18789/healthz` returned JSON within 2 seconds while the local server was listening.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Real external message sending remains disabled; `dryRun=true` remains the default and `dryRun=false` fails closed.\n- The formal pnpm/vitest runner attempted dependency install and was interrupted due the local install/runtime path stalling; direct route/executor checks were used for this bridge scope.",
